  JOURNAL   Cell Metab 33 (12), 2464-2483 (2021)
   PUBMED   34800366
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 3482)
  AUTHORS   Monne,M., Daddabbo,L., Giannossa,L.C., Nicolardi,M.C., Palmieri,L.,
            Miniero,D.V., Mangone,A. and Palmieri,F.
  TITLE     Mitochondrial ATP-Mg/phosphate carriers transport divalent
            inorganic cations in complex with ATP
  JOURNAL   J Bioenerg Biomembr 49 (5), 369-380 (2017)
   PUBMED   28695448
  REMARK    GeneRIF: direct measurements of Mg(2+), Mn(2+), Fe(2+), Zn(2+) and
            Cu(2+) showed that they are cotransported with ATP by both hAPCs
            and AtAPCs. It is likely that in vivo APCs transport free ATP and
            ATP-Mg complex to different degrees, and probably trace amounts of
            other Metals(2+) in complex with ATP.
REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 3482)
  AUTHORS   Sharma,V., Malgulwar,P.B., Purkait,S., Patil,V., Pathak,P.,
            Agrawal,R., Kulshreshtha,R., Mallick,S., Julka,P.K., Suri,A.,
            Sharma,B.S., Suri,V., Sharma,M.C. and Sarkar,C.
  TITLE     Genome-wide ChIP-seq analysis of EZH2-mediated H3K27me3 target gene
            profile highlights differences between low- and high-grade
            astrocytic tumors
  JOURNAL   Carcinogenesis 38 (2), 152-161 (2017)
   PUBMED   27993893
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Our results showed EZH2 to be highly overexpressed in
            astrocytic tumors with a significant positive correlation with
            grade.we identified SLC25A23 as important target of H3K27me3
            modification, which was downregulated in GBM and its low expression
            was associated with poor prognosis in glioblastomas (GBMs).
